my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
do not modify me
END_CODE

{
    desc => 'read-only mode blocks editing',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/readonly_blocks_edit`

Tests that setting the buffer to read-only prevents any text modification.

**initial.png** — Normal mode. Buffer contains `do not modify me`.
The text view has been set to non-editable.

Keys: `i` then type `NOPE` then `<Escape>`

**after_blocked_edit.png** — Buffer content is **unchanged**.
The read-only flag prevented the insert. Still reads `do not modify me`.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->editor->get_textview->set_editable(0);
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->key('i');
        $ctx->type('NOPE');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_blocked_edit');
    },
}
